On 8/24/05, Evgeny Sklyanin <eks2005@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> The problem seems to be with last part of the sentence
> 
> a'o mi pacna lonu se ranji lonu mi benji lo xatra py soi mi
> 
> namely, with
>             mi benji lo xatra py soi mi
> which is rejected by jbofi'e
 
> Seems that jbofi'e does not like {py}. I don't know how to interpret this.

The currently official grammar does not allow free modifiers,
like {soi mi}, following directly after a BY. You need to say
{py boi soi mi}.

(The PEG grammar however has no problem with it.)

